s.0602400103</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B10"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Pacek</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Tutter</surname><given-names>AV</given-names></name><name><surname>Kubota</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name><name><surname>Takisawa</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Walter</surname><given-names>JC</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Localization of MCM2-7, Cdc45, and GINS to the site of DNA unwinding during eukaryotic DNA replication</article-title><source>Mol Cell</source><year>2006</year><volume>21</volume><fpage>581</fpage><lpage>587</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16483939</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/j.molcel.2006.01.030</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B11"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Barry</surname><given-names>ER</given-names></name><name><surname>Bell</surname><given-names>SD</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>DNA replication in the Archaea</article-title><source>Microbiol Mol Biol Rev</source><year>2006</year><volume>70</volume><fpage>876</fpage><lpage>887</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17158702</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1128/MMBR.00029-06</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B12"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Gozuacik</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Chami</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Lagorce</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Faivre</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Murakami</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name><name><surname>Poch</surname><given-names>O</given-names></name><name><surname>Biermann</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Knippers</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Br&#x000e9;chot</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Paterlini-Br&#x000e9;chot</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Identification and functional characterization of a new member of the human Mcm protein family: hMcm8</article-title><source>Nucleic Acids Res</source><year>2003</year><volume>31</volume><fpage>570</fpage><lpage>579</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12527764</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1093/nar/gkg136</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B13"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Maiorano</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Cuvier</surname><given-names>O</given-names></name><name><surname>Danis</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>M&#x000e9;chali</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>MCM8 is an MCM2-7-related protein that functions as a DNA helicase during replication elongation and not initiation</article-title><source>Cell</source><year>2005</year><volume>120</volume><fpage>315</fpage><lpage>328</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15707891</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/j.cell.2004.12.010</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B14"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Volkening</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Hoffmann</surname><given-names>I</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Involvement of human MCM8 in prereplication complex assembly by recruiting hcdc6 to chromatin</article-title><source>Mol Cell Biol</source><year>2005</year><volume>25</volume><fpage>1560</fpage><lpage>1568</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15684404</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1128/MCB.25.4.1560-1568.2005</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B15"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kinoshita</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name><na